 "meter": [
  "ACCEPTED, OR REFUSED \u00b7 AND THE ONE WAY TO CHEAT"
 ],
 "open": [
  false
 ],
 "note": [
  "THE POINT OF THE WHOLE APPROACH IS ON THIS FRAME.\n\nA referee can be tired, generous, or in a hurry. A kernel is none of those. It re-checks every step, and it does not know whose proof it is.\n\nThe right-hand box matters more than it looks. When Lean refuses, it tells you WHICH step it would not take. A 'no' with a specific unmet obligation is a to-do list. A 'no' without one is just a failure. That distinction is why this is worth doing at all.\n\nThen be honest about the escape hatch. 'sorry' means: accept this without proof. It compiles. Anybody can write it. The difference from prose is that it is WRITTEN DOWN - you cannot wave at it, it sits in the file and anybody grepping finds it.\n\nThe four numbers are this repository, counted this morning: sixty-six files, and not one sorry, admit, or new axiom. Say 'counted this morning' - it is the kind of claim you should be able to date."
 ],
